<title>NORWAY: Shareholders approve Aker/Maritime merger.</title>
<headline>Shareholders approve Aker/Maritime merger.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders in Aker ASA and Maritime Group ASA approved on Monday the merger of Aker's Oil and Gas Technology group and Maritime, the companies said in a statement to the Oslo bourse.</p>
<p>Norway's two main suppliers to the oil industry will merge to form a new company, Aker Maritime ASA. The deal is expected to be completed by the end of November, the statement said.</p>
<p>The merged company will have 7,800 employees along the Norwegian coast and another 1,600 in subsidiaries and offices in more than 20 countries.</p>
<p>Aker's oil and gas technology division supplies complete production solutions for offshore oil and gas fields. Maritime Group is a supplier of advanced products and specialised expertise to the oil industry.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
